> **To add your screenshot:** Create a folder named `screenshots` in your repository, upload your dashboard image as `dashboard.png`, and keep the image path above unchanged.

---

##  Project Overview

This project uses Microsoft Excel to transform raw sales data into meaningful business insights. It demonstrates spreadsheet-based data analysis, KPI reporting, data visualization, and business performance monitoring.

The dashboard helps users understand sales trends and compare performance across different business dimensions.

##  Business Objectives

- Monitor total revenue and gross profit.
- Calculate and evaluate gross profit margin.
- Analyze monthly sales performance.
- Compare revenue across countries and regions.
- Evaluate product category and sales channel performance.
- Analyze customer types and units sold.
- Support data-driven business decisions.

##  Tools & Excel Skills

### Data Preparation
- Excel Tables and structured references
- Data organization, sorting, and filtering
- Data validation and consistency checks

### Excel Formulas
- `SUM`, `SUMIF`, `SUMIFS`
- `COUNTIF`, `COUNTIFS`
- `IF`, `IFERROR`, `AVERAGEIFS`
- `XLOOKUP`, `VLOOKUP`, `INDEX-MATCH`
- Date and text functions

### Reporting & Visualization
- PivotTables and PivotCharts
- KPI cards and dashboard design
- Conditional formatting
- Bar, column, line, and combo charts
- Slicers and interactive filtering, where implemented

## Key Performance Indicators (KPIs)

| KPI | Purpose |
|---|---|
| Total Revenue | Measures overall sales value |
| Gross Profit | Measures profit before other business expenses |
| Gross Profit Margin | Measures gross profit as a percentage of revenue |
| Total Units Sold | Measures sales volume |

